VALUES ('13659', 'Criteria Air Pollutants', 'Criteria air pollutants include the six most common air pollutants in the U.S.: carbon monoxide, lead, nitrogen dioxide, ozone, particulate matter, and sulfur dioxide. These pollutants endanger public health and the environment, are widespread throughout the U.S. and come from a variety of sources.  Criteria air pollutants are responsible for many adverse effects on human health, causing thousands of cases of premature mortality and tens of thousands of emergency room visits annually.  They also cause acid rain and can significantly harm ecosystems and the built environment.', 5.00) END
